\source{
Roadmap Epigenomics Project:
\url{https://egg2.wustl.edu/roadmap/web_portal/}

The Roadmap Epigenomics Project provides a comprehensive reference collection
of human epigenomes for key cellular states relevant to human health and
disease. The project generated genome-wide maps of DNA methylation, histone
modifications, chromatin accessibility, and RNA expression across 127
reference epigenomes.

The metadata was originally obtained from the Roadmap Epigenomics web portal
and processed to create this standardized dataset. The data is based on the
\strong{hg19} genome assembly.
}
